| Type of Leave | Entitlement | Key Details |
|---------------|------------|-------------|
| **Annual (Paid) Leave** | **20 days per calendar year** | • Submit requests through the HR portal **at least 5 working days** before the intended start date.<br>• Up to **5 unused days** can be carried forward to the next year. |
| **Sick Leave** | **10 paid days per year** | • Separate from annual leave.<br>• A **medical certificate** is required if the sick leave exceeds **2 consecutive days**. |
| **Public Holidays** | **12 days** (as per the official holiday calendar) | • If you work on a public holiday, you’re eligible for **compensatory leave**. |

**How to Apply**

1. Log in to the **HR portal**.  
2. Choose the appropriate leave type (Annual or Sick).  
3. Enter the dates and provide any required documentation (e.g., medical certificate for extended sick leave).  
4. Submit the request **≥ 5 working days** in advance for annual leave.  

**Carry‑Forward Rule**

- You may roll over **up to 5 unused annual leave days** to the next calendar year. Any excess will be forfeited at year‑end.

If you have any specific scenario or need help with the portal, just let me know!
